{
    "background_story": "Audrey was a historian and archaeologist who spent most of her life studying the rich heritage of Leicester, England. Born and raised in the city, she developed a deep passion for its history, from the Roman walls to the medieval guildhalls. Audrey's most notable achievement was her role in the discovery of King Richard III's remains in a Leicester parking lot. Her meticulous research and persistence helped identify the long-lost king's burial site, sending shockwaves through the academic community. Audrey's work not only shed new light on Leicester's past but also put the city on the global map. She became a local hero, celebrated for her dedication to uncovering the secrets of her beloved city. Audrey's legacy continues to inspire new generations of historians and archaeologists in Leicester.",
